```plaintext
1result.sql
```

Reason: 1result.sql enriches the raw dependency data with a dedicated lookup table (`feature_toggle_libraries`) that maps every relevant artifact to a clean, human‑readable library name and its canonical languages.  
This guarantees:

• exact identification of the requested feature‑toggle artifacts,  
• correct, friendly library names (e.g. “LaunchDarkly”, “Unleash”) instead of repeating the artifact id,  
• accurate library‑language information even when the underlying `projects` table has it blank or misleading,  
• all required repository‑level columns (size converted to bytes, host, fork source, last update, etc.).

The other queries either repeat the artifact as the library name (0result.sql) or infer names/languages heuristically from patterns and the `projects` table, which can mis‑label or miss matches (2result.sql).